# Git line-ending policy.
#
# Every text file is checked out with LF. The local core.autocrlf setting
# rewrites the working tree with CRLF on checkout, which changes the content
# hash the source-audit ledger uses to invalidate stale reviews and breaks
# the shell scripts that Keycloak executes inside its container.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect the binary files (png, svg, drawio) and leave
# them untouched; `eol=lf` forces the line ending of every text file.

* text=auto eol=lf

# The shell scripts are executed by 'sh' inside the Keycloak container. The
# global rule already covers them; the explicit rule documents that they must
# never be rewritten with CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows batch files are binary for Git's line-ending purposes: the cmd.exe
# parser needs CRLF and the file must not be rewritten on checkout.
*.cmd -text
*.bat -text
